{"id":"67D78DBA-6BF8-1014-A85D-F3627178B43A","target_data":{"fqdn":"SOT-WIN2K22-WEB.","mac_address":"00:50:56:36:0D:06","ip_address":"192.168.40.167","role":"Workstation","host_name":"SOT-WIN2K22-WEB","target_type":"Computing"},"stigs":[{"stig_id":"IIS_10-0_Server_STIG","display_name":"Microsoft IIS 10.0 Server","size":40,"rules":[{"rule_id":"SV-218786r1022652","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055","uuid":"67D23CE8-6BF8-1014-99AC-BA6BD476E8FE","discussion":"Internet Information Services (IIS) on Windows Server 2012 provides basic logging capabilities. However, because IIS takes some time to flush logs to disk, administrators do not have access to logging information in real-time. In addition, text-based log files can be difficult and time-consuming to process.\n\nIn IIS 10.0, the administrator has the option of sending logging information to Event Tracing for Windows (ETW). This option gives the administrator the ability to use standard query tools, or create custom tools, for viewing real-time logging information in ETW. This provides a significant advantage over parsing text-based log files that are not updated in real time.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055, SRG-APP-000108-WSR-000166, SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000063","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.logFile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878601 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878601 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.logFile.logTargetW3C'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878601 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal File, ETW\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'File, ETW'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.logFile.logTargetW3C'\n                        : result equals 'File'\n\nResult Analysis         : Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.logFile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n","ccis":["CCI-000139","CCI-001464","CCI-001851"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218786","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218786r1022652_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 server name.\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\nUnder Log Event Destination, verify the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button is selected.\n\nIf the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button is not selected, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 server name.\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nUnder Log Event Destination, select the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button.\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane, click \"Apply\".","group_id":"V-218786","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218786","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000103","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218786","title":"SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109211","V-100107"],"comments":null,"mitigations":""},{"check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\nSelect \"Fields\".\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", verify the following fields have been configured:\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Connection.\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Warning.\nIf any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\nSelect \"Fields\".\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", click \"Add Field...\".\nFor each field being added, give a name unique to what the field is capturing.\nClick on the \"Source Type\" drop-down list and select \"Request Header\".\nClick the \"Source\" drop-down list, and select \"Connection\".\nClick \"OK\" to add.\n\nClick the \"Source Type\" drop-down list, and select \"Request Header\".\nClick the \"Source\" drop-down list, and select \"Warning\".\nClick \"OK\" to add.\nClick \"Apply\" under the \"Actions\" pane.","uuid":"67D2498C-6BF8-1014-9221-F82BD8DECE8C","group_title":"SRG-APP-000099-WSR-000061","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must produce log records that contain sufficient information to establish the outcome (success or failure) of IIS 10.0 web server events.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218788r1156543","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218788","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218788r1156543_rule","ccis":["CCI-000134"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false ((Custom Fields - Request Header - Connection) Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the Logging icon. Verify the Format: under Log File is configured to W3C. Select the Fields button. Under Custom Fields, verify the following fields have been configured: Request Header - Connection Request Header - Warning Server Variable - HTTP_CONNECTION If any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((Custom Fields - Request Header - Warning) Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the Logging icon. Verify the Format: under Log File is configured to W3C. Select the Fields button. Under Custom Fields, verify the following fields have been configured: Request Header - Connection Request Header - Warning Server Variable - HTTP_CONNECTION If any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   true (Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878801 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (Custom Fields - Request Header - Connection) Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the Logging icon. Verify the Format: under Log File is configured to W3C. Select the Fields button. Under Custom Fields, verify the following fields have been configured: Request Header - Connection Request Header - Warning Server Variable - HTTP_CONNECTION If any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878801 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieve IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'WebAdministration'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'WebConfigurationProperty'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : filter must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults/logFile/customFields/add'\n                        : name must be equal to '.'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'logFieldName,sourceType,sourceName'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878801 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Verify IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields - Request Header - Connection Enabled\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all sourcetype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'RequestHeader'\n                        : all sourcename must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Connection'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878802 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (Custom Fields - Request Header - Warning) Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the Logging icon. Verify the Format: under Log File is configured to W3C. Select the Fields button. Under Custom Fields, verify the following fields have been configured: Request Header - Connection Request Header - Warning Server Variable - HTTP_CONNECTION If any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878801 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieve IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'WebAdministration'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'WebConfigurationProperty'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : filter must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults/logFile/customFields/add'\n                        : name must be equal to '.'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'logFieldName,sourceType,sourceName'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878802 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Verify IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields - Request Header - Warning Enabled\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all sourcetype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'RequestHeader'\n                        : all sourcename must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Warning'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878803 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878802 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.logFile.logFormat'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878803 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal W3C\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.logFile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Web server logging capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without sufficient and accurate information, a correct replay of the events cannot be determined.\n\nAscertaining the success or failure of an event is important during forensic analysis. Correctly determining the outcome will add information to the overall reconstruction of the loggable event. By determining the success or failure of the event correctly, analysis of the enterprise can be undertaken to determine if events tied to the event occurred in other areas within the enterprise.\n\nWithout sufficient information establishing the success or failure of the logged event, investigation into the cause of event is severely hindered. The success or failure also provides a means to measure the impact of an event and help authorized personnel determine the appropriate response. Log record content that may be necessary to satisfy the requirement of this control includes, but is not limited to, time stamps, source and destination IP addresses, user/process identifiers, event descriptions, application-specific events, success/fail indications, file names involved, access control, or flow control rules invoked.","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000110","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109215","V-100111"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000099-WSR-000061","id":"V-218788"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218788","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218788"},{"uuid":"67D251CB-6BF8-1014-B131-E70D6CAC2DFB","group_title":"SRG-APP-000100-WSR-000064","rule_id":"SV-218789r1156546","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must produce log records containing sufficient information to establish the identity of any user/subject or process associated with an event.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001487"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218789","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218789r1156546_rule","discussion":"Web server logging capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without sufficient and accurate information, a correct replay of the events cannot be determined.\n\nDetermining user accounts, processes running on behalf of the user, and running process identifiers also enable a better understanding of the overall event. User tool identification is also helpful to determine if events are related to overall user access or specific client tools.\n\nLog record content that may be necessary to satisfy the requirement of this control includes: time stamps, source and destination addresses, user/process identifiers, event descriptions, success/fail indications, file names involved, and access control or flow control rules invoked.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C)\nTest                    :   true ((Standard Field - User Agent) )\nTest                    :   true ((User Name Field) Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Click the Logging icon. Under Format select W3C. Click Select Fields, verify at a minimum the following fields are checked: Date, Time, Client IP Address, User Name, Method, URI Query, Protocol Status, and Referrer. If not, this is a finding.)\nTest                    :   true ((Referrer Field) Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Click the Logging icon. Under Format select W3C. Click Select Fields, verify at a minimum the following fields are checked: Date, Time, Client IP Address, User Name, Method, URI Query, Protocol Status, and Referrer. If not, this is a finding.)\nTest                    :   false ((Custom Fields - Request Header - Authorization) )\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((Custom Fields - Response Header - Content-Type) )\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878901 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878901 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.logFile.logFormat'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878901 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal W3C\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.logFile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878902 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : (Standard Field - User Agent) \nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878902 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : The enhanced logging for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled and capture all user and web server events.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/log'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878902 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : Verify IIS Webserver Logging standard Fields - UserAgent\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'UserAgent'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/log'\n                        : parameter equals 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, SiteName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878903 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : (User Name Field) Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Click the Logging icon. Under Format select W3C. Click Select Fields, verify at a minimum the following fields are checked: Date, Time, Client IP Address, User Name, Method, URI Query, Protocol Status, and Referrer. If not, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878902 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : The enhanced logging for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled and capture all user and web server events.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/log'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878903 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must include UserName.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'UserName'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/log'\n                        : parameter equals 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, SiteName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878904 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : (Referrer Field) Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Click the Logging icon. Under Format select W3C. Click Select Fields, verify at a minimum the following fields are checked: Date, Time, Client IP Address, User Name, Method, URI Query, Protocol Status, and Referrer. If not, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878902 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : The enhanced logging for the IIS 10.0 web server must be enabled and capture all user and web server events.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/log'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878904 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must include Referer.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Referer'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/log'\n                        : parameter equals 'centralW3CLogFile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, SiteName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878905 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (Custom Fields - Request Header - Authorization) \nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878903 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieve IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'WebAdministration'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'WebConfigurationProperty'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : filter must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults/logFile/customFields/add'\n                        : name must be equal to '.'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'logFieldName,sourceType,sourceName'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878905 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Verify IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields - Request Header - Authorization\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all sourcetype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'RequestHeader'\n                        : all sourcename must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Authorization'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21878906 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (Custom Fields - Response Header - Content-Type) \nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21878903 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieve IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'WebAdministration'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'WebConfigurationProperty'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : filter must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults/logFile/customFields/add'\n                        : name must be equal to '.'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'logFieldName,sourceType,sourceName'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21878906 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Verify IIS Webserver Logging Custom Fields - Response Header - Content-Type\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all sourcetype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'ResponseHeader'\n                        : all sourcename must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Content-Type'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\nSelect \"Fields\".\nUnder \"Standard Fields\", verify \"User Agent\", \"User Name\", and \"Referrer\" are selected.\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", verify the following field has been configured:\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Authorization.\nResponse Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type.\nIf any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\nSelect \"Fields\".\nUnder \"Standard Fields\", select \"User Agent\", \"User Name\", and \"Referrer\".\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", select the following fields:\nClick the \"Source Type\" drop-down list, and select \"Request Header\".\nClick on \"Source\" drop-down, list and select \"Authorization\".\nClick \"OK\" to add.\n\nClick the \"Source\" drop-down list, and select \"Content-Type\".\nClick the \"Source Type\" drop-down list, and select \"Response Header\".\nClick \"OK\" to add.\nClick \"OK\".\nClick \"Apply\" under the \"Actions\" pane.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218789","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-218789","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000111","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":["SV-109217","V-100113"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218789","title":"SRG-APP-000100-WSR-000064"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"uuid":"67D2598B-6BF8-1014-8CE4-F3F1C186AFB7","group_title":"SRG-APP-000125-WSR-000071","rule_id":"SV-218791r960948","rule_title":"The log data and records from the IIS 10.0 web server must be backed up onto a different system or media.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001348"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:701","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218791r960948_rule","discussion":"Protection of log data includes ensuring log data is not accidentally lost or deleted. Backing up log records to an unrelated system, or onto separate media than the system on which the web server is running, helps to ensure the log records will be retained in the event of a catastrophic system failure.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218791, SV-218791r960948, SRG-APP-000125-WSR-000071)\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"The IIS 10.0 web server and website log files should be backed up by the system backup.\n\nTo determine if log files are backed up by the system backup, determine the location of the web server log files and each website's log files.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 server name.\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nUnder \"Log File\" &gt;&gt; \"Directory\" obtain the path of the log file.\n\nOnce all locations are known, consult with the System Administrator to review the server's backup procedure and policy.\n\nVerify the paths of all log files are part of the system backup.\nVerify log files are backed up to an unrelated system or onto separate media on which the system the web server is running.\n\nIf the paths of all log files are not part of the system backup and/or not backed up to a separate media, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure system backups to include the directory paths of all IIS 10.0 web server and website log files.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218791","group_id":"V-218791","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000116","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":["SV-109221","V-100117"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000125-WSR-000071","id":"V-218791"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"rule_id":"SV-218792r960963","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must not perform user management for hosted applications.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D260BE-6BF8-1014-9891-EF1936FC01AC","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000015","discussion":"User management and authentication can be an essential part of any application hosted by the web server. Along with authenticating users, the user management function must perform several other tasks enterprise-wide, such as password complexity, locking users after a configurable number of failed logons, and management of temporary and emergency accounts.\n\nThe web server contains a minimal user management function, but the web server user management function does not offer enterprise-wide user management, and user management is not the primary function of the web server. User management for the hosted applications should be done through a facility built for enterprise-wide user management, such as LDAP and Active Directory.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218792, SV-218792r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000015)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:901","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218792r960963_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator about the role of the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is hosting an application, have the SA provide supporting documentation on how the application's user management is accomplished outside of the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is not hosting an application, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the IIS web server is performing user management for hosted applications, this is a finding.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is hosting an application and the SA cannot provide supporting documentation on how the application's user management is accomplished outside of the IIS 10.0 web server, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Reconfigure any hosted applications on the IIS 10.0 web server to perform user management outside the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nDocument how the hosted application user management is accomplished.","group_id":"V-218792","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218792","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000117","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109223","V-100119"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000015","id":"V-218792"},"mitigations":""},{"discussion":"A web server can provide many features, services, and processes. Some of these may be deemed unnecessary or too unsecure to run on a production DoD system.\n\nThe web server must provide the capability to disable, uninstall, or deactivate functionality and services deemed non-essential to the web server mission or that adversely impact server performance.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218793, SV-218793r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218793r960963_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:1101"},"rule_id":"SV-218793r960963","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must only contain functions necessary for operation.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D267DC-6BF8-1014-BCEB-DEA40FEBFC25","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove all unapproved programs and roles from the production IIS 10.0 web server.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Click âStartâ.\n\nOpen Control Panel.\n\nClick âProgramsâ.\n\nClick âPrograms and Featuresâ.\n\nReview the installed programs. If any programs are installed other than those required for the IIS 10.0 web services, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If additional software is needed, supporting documentation must be signed by the ISSO.","group_id":"V-218793","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218793","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109225","V-100121"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218793","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000118","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nUnder the \"Connections\" pane on the left side of the management console, select the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nUnder the IIS installed features, if \"Application Request Routing Cache\" is present, double-click the icon to open the feature.\n\nFrom the right \"Actions\" pane, under \"Proxy\", select \"Server Proxy Settings...\".\n\nIn the \"Application Request Routing\" settings window, remove the check from the \"Enable proxy\" check box.\n\nClick \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nUnder the \"Connections\" pane on the left side of the management console, select the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nIf, under the IIS installed features \"Application Request Routing Cache\" is not present, this is not a finding.\n\nIf, under the IIS installed features \"Application Request Routing Cache\" is present, double-click the icon to open the feature.\n\nFrom the right \"Actions\" pane under \"Proxy\", select \"Server Proxy Settings...\".\n\nIn the \"Application Request Routing\" settings window, verify whether \"Enable proxy\" is selected.\n\nIf \"Enable proxy\" is selected under the \"Application Request Routing\" settings, this is a finding.\n\nIf the server has been approved to be a Proxy server, this requirement is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218794"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218794r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Application Request Routing Cache - Installation Status.)\nTest                    :   false (Application Request Routing Cache - Proxy Enable Setting)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879402 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Application Request Routing Cache - Installation Status.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879401 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Application Request Routing Cache - Proxy Enable Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/proxy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'enabled'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879401 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Application Request Routing Cache - Proxy Enable Setting\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879401 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Application Request Routing Cache - Proxy Enable Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/proxy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21879401 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\n","discussion":"A web server should be primarily a web server or a proxy server but not both, for the same reasons that other multi-use servers are not recommended. Scanning for web servers that also proxy requests into an otherwise protected network is a common attack, making the attack anonymous.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000076","uuid":"67D26ED0-6BF8-1014-8EAD-D6DA9F3045D3","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must not be both a website server and a proxy server.","rule_id":"SV-218794r960963","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000076","id":"V-218794"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109227","V-100123"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000119","group_id_src":"V-218794","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218794"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove any executable sample code, example applications, or tutorials which are not explicitly used by a production website.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Navigate to the following folders:\n\ninetpub\\\nProgram Files\\Common Files\\System\\msadc\nProgram Files (x86)\\Common Files\\System\\msadc\n\nIf the folder or sub-folders contain any executable sample code, example applications, or tutorials which are not explicitly used by a production website, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (.hlp,.htm,.asp file extensions shall not exist)\nResult Analysis         :        Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 57 collected items exist, so result is false\nTest                    :   true (.hlp,.htm,.asp file extensions shall not exist)\nTest                    :   true (.hlp,.htm,.asp file extensions shall not exist)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879501 (file_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : .hlp,.htm,.asp file extensions shall not exist\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879501 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : The following file extensions must not exist: asp,htm,hlp\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      : for path, at least one of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     path must be equal to 'C:\\Inetpub\\'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '^.*\\.([Aa][Ss][Pp]|[Hh][Tt][Mm]|[Hh][Ll][Pp])$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\inetpub\\custerr\\en-US\\401-1.htm'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\inetpub\\custerr\\en-US'\n                        : filename equals '401-1.htm'\n                        : owner equals 'NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM'\n                        : size equals '1297'\n                        : a_time equals '133513674670000000'\n                        : c_time equals '133513674680000000'\n                        : m_time equals '133513674670000000'\n                        : ms_checksum does not exist\n                        : version does not exist\n                        : type equals 'FILE_TYPE_DISK'\n                        : attribute equals 'FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ARCHIVE'\n                        : development_class does not exist\n                        : company does not exist\n                        : internal_name does not exist\n                        : language does not exist\n                        : original_filename does not exist\n                        : product_name does not exist\n                        : product_version does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\inetpub\\custerr\\en-US\\401-2.htm'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\inetpub\\custerr\\en-US'\n                        : filename equals '401-2.htm'\n                        : owner equals 'NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM'\n                        : size equals '1415'\n                        : a_time equals '133513674670000000'\n                        : c_time equals '133513674680000000'\n                        : m_time equals '133513674670000000'\n                        : ms_checksum does not exis