 may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879502 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : asp,htm,hlp\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      : for path, at least one of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     path must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Common Files\\System\\msadc\\'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '^.*\\.([Aa][Ss][Pp]|[Hh][Tt][Mm]|[Hh][Ll][Pp])$'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879503 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : .hlp,.htm,.asp file extensions shall not exist\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879503 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : asp,htm,hlp\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      : for path, at least one of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     path must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Common Files\\System\\msadc\\'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '^.*\\.([Aa][Ss][Pp]|[Hh][Tt][Mm]|[Hh][Ll][Pp])$'\n","discussion":"Web server documentation, sample code, example applications, and tutorials may be an exploitable threat to a web server. A production web server may only contain components that are operationally necessary (i.e., compiled code, scripts, web content, etc.). Delete all directories containing samples and any scripts used to execute the samples.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218795"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218795r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"All IIS 10.0 web server sample code, example applications, and tutorials must be removed from a production IIS 10.0 server.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218795r960963","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000077","uuid":"67D278ED-6BF8-1014-9E2A-C4E526770981","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000077","id":"V-218795"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109229","V-100125"],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000120","reference_identifier":"4052","severity":"high","group_id":"V-218795","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218795","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":""},{"check_content":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nAccess âAppsâ menu. Under âAdministrative Toolsâ, select âComputer Managementâ.\n\nIn the left pane, expand \"Local Users and Groups\" and click \"Users\".\n\nReview the local users listed in the middle pane.\n\nIf any local accounts are present and were created by features which have been uninstalled or are not used, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nAccess âAppsâ menu. Under âAdministrative Toolsâ, select âComputer Managementâ.\n\nIn the left pane, expand \"Local Users and Groups\" and click \"Users\".\n\nDelete any local accounts which were created by features which have been uninstalled or are not used.","uuid":"67D281ED-6BF8-1014-9DD5-BC03867A142D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000078","rule_id":"SV-218796r960963","rule_title":"The accounts created by uninstalled features (i.e., tools, utilities, specific, etc.) must be deleted from the IIS 10.0 server.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:1701","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218796r960963_rule","discussion":"Accounts used for web server features such as documentation, sample code, example applications, tutorials, utilities, and services created when the feature is not installed, become an exploitable threat to a web server.\n\nThese accounts become inactive, are not monitored through regular use, and passwords for the accounts are not created or updated. An attacker, through very little effort, can use these accounts to gain access to the web server and begin investigating ways to elevate the account privileges.\n\nThe accounts used for web server features not installed must not be created and must be deleted when these features are uninstalled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218796, SV-218796r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000078)\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000121","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109231","V-100127"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000078","id":"V-218796"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218796","group_id":"V-218796","severity":"medium"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove all utility programs, Operating System features, or modules installed that are not necessary for web server operation.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Consult with the System Administrator and review all of the IIS 10.0 and Operating System features installed.\n\nDetermine if any features installed are no longer necessary for operation.\n\nIf any utility programs, features, or modules are installed which are not necessary for operation, this is a finding.\n\nIf any unnecessary Operating System features are installed, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218797, SV-218797r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080)\n","discussion":"Just as running unneeded services and protocols is a danger to the web server at the lower levels of the OSI model, running unneeded utilities and programs is a danger at the application layer of the OSI model. Office suites, development tools, and graphic editors are examples of such troublesome programs.\n\nIndividual productivity tools have no legitimate place or use on an enterprise production web server and are prone to security risks. The web server installation process must provide options allowing the installer to choose which utility programs, services, and modules are to be installed or removed. By having a process for installation and removal, the web server is guaranteed to be in a more stable and secure state than if these services and programs were installed and removed manually.","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:1901"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218797r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must be reviewed on a regular basis to remove any Operating System features, utility programs, plug-ins, and modules not necessary for operation.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218797r960963","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080","uuid":"67D28949-6BF8-1014-9F1C-995AD4B255CD","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080","id":"V-218797"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109233","V-100129"],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000123","reference_identifier":"4052","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218797","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218797","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109235","V-100131"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081","id":"V-218798"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000124","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","group_id":"V-218798","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218798","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder IIS, double-click the \"MIME Types\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Group by:\" drop-down list, select \"Content Type\".\n\nFrom the list of extensions under \"Application\", remove MIME types for OS shell program extensions, to include at a minimum, the following extensions:\n\n.exe\n.dll\n.com\n.bat\n.csh\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane, click \"Apply\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder IIS, double-click the \"MIME Types\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Group by:\" drop-down list, select \"Content Type\".\n\nFrom the list of extensions under \"Application\", verify MIME types for OS shell program extensions have been removed, to include at a minimum, the following extensions:\n\n.exe\n.dll\n.com\n.bat\n.csh\n\nIf any OS shell MIME types are configured, this is a finding.","discussion":"Controlling what a user of a hosted application can access is part of the security posture of the web server. Any time a user can access more functionality than is needed for the operation of the hosted application poses a security issue. A user with too much access can view information that is not needed for the user's job role, or the user could use the function in an unintentional manner.\n\nA MIME tells the web server the type of program, various file types, and extensions and what external utilities or programs are needed to execute the file type.\n\nA shell is a program that serves as the basic interface between the user and the operating system to ensure hosted application users do not have access to these programs. Shell programs may execute shell escapes and can perform unauthorized activities that could damage the security posture of the web server.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the âMIME Typesâ icon. From the Group by: drop-down list, select Content Type. From the list of extensions under Application, verify MIME types for OS shell program extensions have been removed, to include at a minimum, the following extensions: .exe .dll .com .bat .csh If any OS shell MIME types are configured, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879801 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Open the IIS 10.0 Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 web server name. Under IIS, double-click the âMIME Typesâ icon. From the Group by: drop-down list, select Content Type. From the list of extensions under Application, verify MIME types for OS shell program extensions have been removed, to include at a minimum, the following extensions: .exe .dll .com .bat .csh If any OS shell MIME types are configured, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : No collected item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879801 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Site Default Logfile format must be set to W3C\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/staticContent'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'all'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21879801 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : remove MIME types for OS shell program extensions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern '\\[mimeMap\\]\\s+fileExtension:\"\\.(exe|dll|com|bat|csh)\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/staticContent'\n                        : parameter equals 'all'\n                        : result equals 'CONFIG   CONFIG.SECTION:\"system.webServer/staticContent\"   path:\"MACHINE/WEBROOT/APPHOST\"   overrideMode:\"Inherit\"   locked:\"false\"   [system.webServer/staticContent]      defaultDocFooter:\"\"      isDocFooterFileName:\"false\"      enableDocFooter:\"false\"      [clientCache]        cacheControlMode:\"NoControl\"        cacheControlMaxAge:\"1.00:00:00\"        httpExpires:\"\"        cacheControlCustom:\"\"        setEtag:\"true\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".323\"        mimeType:\"text/h323\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".3g2\"        mimeType:\"video/3gpp2\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".3gp2\"        mimeType:\"video/3gpp2\"      