omments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000125","reference_identifier":"4052","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218799","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218799","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access Server Manager on the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nClick on \"Manage\".\n\nSelect \"Add Roles and Features\".\n\nClick \"Next\" in the \"Before you begin\" dialog box.\n\nSelect \"Role-based or feature-based installation\" on the \"Installation Type\" dialog box and click \"Next\".\n\nSelect the IIS 10.0 web server in the \"Server Selection\" dialog box.\n\nFrom the \"Windows Features\" dialog box, navigate to \"World Wide Web Services\" &gt;&gt; \"Common HTTP Features\".\n\nDe-select \"WebDAV Publishing\", and click \"Next\" to complete removing the WebDAV Publishing feature from the IIS 10.0 web server.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nReview the features listed under the âIIS\" section.\n\nIf the \"WebDAV Authoring Rules\" icon exists, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Verify IIS WebDAV Authoring Rules is not installed via registry test)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21879901 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify IIS WebDAV Authoring Rules is not installed via registry test\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21879901 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Verify IIS WebDAV Authoring Rules is not installed via registry test\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\InetStp\\Components'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'WebDAV'\n","discussion":"A web server can be installed with functionality that by its nature is not secure. Web Distributed Authoring (WebDAV) is an extension to the HTTP protocol which, when developed, was meant to allow users to create, change, and move documents on a server, typically a web server or web share. Allowing this functionality, development, and deployment is much easier for web authors.\n\nWebDAV is not widely used and has serious security concerns because it may allow clients to modify unauthorized files on the web server.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218799"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218799r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must have Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) disabled.","rule_id":"SV-218799r960963","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000085","uuid":"67D298F7-6BF8-1014-AB76-ABEE101B7A15"},{"reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000130","group_tree":{"id":"V-218801","title":"SRG-APP-000206-WSR-000128"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109241","V-100137"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218801","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218801","severity":"medium","check_content":"Search the system for files with either .java or .jpp extensions.\n\nIf files with .java or .jpp extensions are found, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove all files from the web server with both .java and .jpp extensions.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206-WSR-000128","uuid":"67D2A05F-6BF8-1014-AF01-C97F134585D6","rule_id":"SV-218801r961083","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Java software installed on a production IIS 10.0 web server must be limited to .class files and the Java Virtual Machine.","potential_impacts":"","ccis":["CCI-001166"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218801"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218801r961083_rule","discussion":"Mobile code in hosted applications allows the developer to add functionality and displays to hosted applications that are fluid, as opposed to a static web page. The data presentation becomes more appealing to the user, is easier to analyze, and is less complicated to navigate through the hosted application and data.\n\nSome mobile code technologies in use in today's applications are: Java, JavaScript, ActiveX, PDF, Postscript, Shockwave movies, Flash animations, and VBScript. The DoD has created policies that define the usage of mobile code on DoD systems. The usage restrictions and implementation guidance apply to both the selection and use of mobile code installed on organizational servers and mobile code downloaded and executed on individual workstations.\n\nSource code for a Java program is often stored in files with either .java or .jpp file extensions. From the .java and .jpp files the Java compiler produces a binary file with an extension of .class. The .java or .jpp file could therefore reveal sensitive information regarding an application's logic and permissions to resources on the server.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If files with .java or .jpp extensions are found, this is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21880101 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If files with .java or .jpp extensions are found, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21880101 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : If files with .java or .jpp extensions are found, this is a finding.\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'path' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '^.*\\.([Jj][Aa][Vv][Aa]|[Jj][Pp][Pp])$'\n"},{"fix_text":"Ensure non-administrators are not allowed access to the directory tree, the shell, or other operating system functions and utilities.\n\nAll non-administrator access to shell scripts and operating system functions must be mission essential and documented.","documentable":"false","check_content":"Obtain a list of the user accounts with access to the system, including all local and domain accounts. \n\nReview the privileges to the web server for each account.\n\nVerify with the system administrator or the ISSO that all privileged accounts are mission essential and documented.\n\nVerify with the system administrator or the ISSO that all non-administrator access to shell scripts and operating system functions are mission essential and documented.\n\nIf undocumented privileged accounts are found, this is a finding.\n\nIf undocumented non-administrator access to shell scripts and operating system functions are found, this is a finding.\n\nIf this IIS 10 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-218802r1138072_rule","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:2701"},"ccis":["CCI-001082"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-218802, SV-218802r1138072, SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000030)\n","discussion":"As a rule, accounts on a web server are to be kept to a minimum. Only administrators, web managers, developers, auditors, and web authors require accounts on the machine hosting the web server. This is in addition to the anonymous web user account. The resources to which these accounts have access must also be closely monitored and controlled. Only the SA needs access to all the systemâs capabilities, while the web administrator and associated staff require access and control of the web content and web server configuration files. The anonymous web user account must not have access to system resources as that account could then control the server.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000030","uuid":"67D2A793-6BF8-1014-81AB-F8E11C64859F","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"IIS 10.0 Web server accounts accessing the directory tree, the shell, or other operating system functions and utilities must only be administrative accounts.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218802r1138072","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000030","id":"V-218802"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109243","V-100139"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000131","group_id_src":"V-218802","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"high","group_id":"V-218802"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129","id":"V-218803"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109245","V-100141"],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000132","reference_identifier":"4052","group_id":"V-218803","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218803","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Develop a method to manage the hosted applications, either by moving its management functions off of the IIS 10.0 web server or by accessing the application's management via a uniquely assigned IP address.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Review the IIS 10.0 web server configuration with the System Administrator.\n\nDetermine if the IIS 10.0 web server hosts any applications.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server does not host any applications, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is hosting Exchange, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server hosts applications, review the application's management functionality and authentication methods with the System Administrator to determine if the management of the application is accomplished with the same functions and authentication methods as the web server management.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server management and the application's management functionality is not separated, this is a finding.","discussion":"The separation of user functionality from web server management can be accomplished by moving management functions to a separate IP address or port. To further separate the management functions, separate authentication methods and certificates should be used.\n\nBy moving the management functionality, the possibility of accidental discovery of the management functions by non-privileged users during hosted application use is minimized.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218803, SV-218803r1138074, SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129)\n","ccis":["CCI-001082"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:2901"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218803r1138074_rule","rule_id":"SV-218803r1138074","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must separate the hosted applications from hosted web server management functionality.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129","uuid":"67D2AEC3-6BF8-1014-8CBD-9333CC78DC40"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218804","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218804","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109247","V-100143"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000223-WSR-000011","id":"V-218804"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000134","weight":"10.0","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218804","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218804r1043180_rule","ccis":["CCI-001664"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Cookies are used to exchange data between the web server and the client. Cookies, such as a session cookie, may contain session information and user credentials used to maintain a persistent connection between the user and the hosted application since HTTP/HTTPS is a stateless protocol.\n\nUsing URI will embed the session ID as a query string in the Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) request and then the URI is redirected to the originally requested URL. The changed URI request is used for the duration of the session, so no cookie is necessary.\n\nBy requiring expired session IDs to be regenerated while using URI, potential attackers have less time to capture a cookie and gain access to the Web server content.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000223-WSR-000011, SRG-APP-000220-WSR-000201","uuid":"67D2B5CE-6BF8-1014-9181-B1E744F3A3D8","group_title":"SRG-APP-000223-WSR-000011","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must use cookies to track session state.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218804r1043180","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"ASP.Net\", double-click the \"Session State\" icon.\n\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", select \"Use Cookiesâ from the \"Mode\" drop-down list.\n\nClick \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nUnder \"ASP.Net\", double-click the \"Session State\" icon.\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", verify the \"Mode\" has \"Use Cookies\" selected from the drop-down list.\nIf the \"Cookie Settings\" \"Mode\" is not set to \"Use Cookies\", this is a finding.\n\nAlternative method:\nClick the site name.\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\".\nVerify the \"cookieless\" is set to \"UseCookies\".\nIf the \"cookieless\" is not set to \"UseCookies\", this is a finding.\n\nNote: If IIS 10.0 server/site is used only for system-to-system maintenance, does not allow users to connect to interface, and is restricted to specific system IPs, this is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218805","group_id_src":"V-218805","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218805","title":"SRG-APP-000223-WSR-000145"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109249","V-100145"],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000135","reference_identifier":"4052","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"ASP.NET provides a session state, which is available as the HttpSessionState class, as a method of storing session-specific information that is visible only within the session. ASP.NET session state identifies requests from the same browser during a limited time window as a session and provides the ability to persist variable values for the duration of that session.\n\nWhen using the URI mode for cookie settings under session state, IIS will reject and reissue session IDs that do not have active sessions. Configuring IIS to expire session IDs and regenerate tokens gives a potential attacker less time to capture a cookie and gain access to server content.","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218805"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218805r1067583_rule","ccis":["CCI-001664"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must accept only system-generated session identifiers.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218805r1067583","group_title":"SRG-APP-000223-WSR-000145","uuid":"67D2BD2E-6BF8-1014-83B9-C849DEC6A5B5","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder the \"ASP.NET\" section, select \"Session State\".\n\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", select the \"Use Cookies\" mode from the \"Mode:\" drop-down list.\n\nUnder \"Time-out (in minutes)\", enter a value of \"15 or less\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder the \"ASP.NET\" section, select \"Session State\".\n\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", verify the \"Use Cookies\" mode is selected from the \"Mode:\" drop-down list.\n\nUnder \"Time-out (in minutes)\", verify a maximum of 15 minutes is entered.\n\nIf the \"Use Cookies\" mode is selected and Time-out (in minutes) is configured for \"15 minutes\" (or less), this is not a finding.\n\nAlternative method:\n\nClick the site name.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\".\n\nVerify the \"cookieless\" is set to \"UseCookies\".\n\nIf the \"cookieless\" is not set to \"UseCookies\", this is a finding.\n\nNote: If IIS 10.0 server/site is used only for system-to-system maintenance, does not allow users to connect to interface, and is restricted to specific system IPs, this is Not Applicable."},{"rule_id":"SV-218806r961122","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must augment re-creation to a stable and known baseline.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D2C741-6BF8-1014-943A-A47D5E00D9E5","group_title":"SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000074","discussion":"Making certain that the web server has not been updated by an unauthorized user is always a concern. Adding patches, functions, and modules that are untested and not part of the baseline opens the possibility for security risks. The web server must offer, and not hinder, a method that allows for the quick and easy reinstallation of a verified and patched baseline to guarantee the production web server is up-to-date and has not been modified to add functionality or expose security risks.\n\nWhen the web server does not offer a method to roll back to a clean baseline, external methods, such as a baseline snapshot or virtualizing the web server, can be used.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218806, SV-218806r961122, SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000074)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001190"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:3501"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218806r961122_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator for the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nAsk for documentation on the disaster recovery methods tested and planned for the IIS 10.0 web server in the event of the necessity for rollback.\n\nIf documentation for a disaster recovery has not been established, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Prepare documentation for disaster recovery methods for the IIS 10.0 web server in the event of the necessity for rollback.\n\nDocument and test the disaster recovery methods designed.","group_id":"V-218806","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218806","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000136","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-109251","V-100147"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218806","title":"SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000074"},"mitigations":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218807","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218807","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109253","V-100149"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218807","title":"SRG-APP-000231-WSR-000144"},"rule_version":"IIST-SV-000137","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The Machine Key element of the ASP.NET web.config specifies the algorithm and keys that ASP.NET will use for encryption. The Machine Key feature can be managed to specify hashing and encryption settings for application services such as view state, forms authentication, membership and roles, and anonymous identification. Ensuring a strong encryption method can mitigate the risk of data tampering in crucial functional areas such as forms authentication cookies, or view state.","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218807"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218807r1067586_rule","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The production IIS 10.0 web server must utilize SHA2 encryption for the Machine Key.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218807r1067586","uuid":"67D2CF84-6BF8-1014-B32C-E5181C782A2A","group_title":"SRG-APP-000231-WSR-000144","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Machine Key\" icon in the web server Home Pane.\n\nSet the Validation method to \"HMACSHA256\" or stronger.\n\nSet the Encryption method to \"Auto\".\n\nClick \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nNote: If the IIS 10.0 web server is hosting Exchange, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Machine Key\" icon in the website Home Pane.\n\nVerify \"HMACSHA256\" or stronger encryption is selected for the Validation method and \"Auto\" is selected for the Encryption method.\n\nIf \"HMACSHA256\" or stronger encryption is not selected for the Validation method and/or \"Auto\" is not selected for the Encryption method, this is a finding.\n\nIf .NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable."},{"reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000138","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000251-WSR-000157","id":"V-218808"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109255","V-100151"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218808","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218808","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Directory Browsing\" icon.\n\nUnder the âActionsâ pane verify \"Directory Browsing\" is disabled.\n\nIf âDirectory Browsingâ is not disabled, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Directory Browsing\" icon.\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane click \"Disabled\".\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane, click \"Apply\".","group_title":"SRG-APP-000251-WSR-000157","uuid":"67D2D6DA-6BF8-1014-9324-9C7374580490","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Directory Browsing on the IIS 10.0 web server must be disabled.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218808r961158","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218808","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218808r961158_rule","ccis":["CCI-001310"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Verify Directory Browsing is not enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21880801 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify Directory Browsing is not enabled\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21880801 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Directory Browsing Webserver Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'directoryBrowse'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21880801 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'directoryBrowse'\n                        : parameter equals 'enabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","discussion":"Directory browsing allows the contents of a directory to be displayed upon request from a web client. If directory browsing is enabled for a directory in IIS, users could receive a web page listing the contents of the directory. If directory browsing is enabled, the risk of inadvertently disclosing sensitive content is increased."},{"stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218810","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218810","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"id":"V-218810","title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109259","V-100155"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000140","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218810"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218810r1022657_rule","discussion":"HTTP error pages contain information that could enable an attacker to gain access to an information system. Failure to prevent the sending of HTTP error pages with full information to remote requesters exposes internal configuration information to potential attackers.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Webserver Error Pages - Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests must be selected)\nTest                    :   false (Webserver Error Pages - Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests must be selected)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881001 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Webserver Error Pages - Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests must be selected\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver Error Pages Error Response Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'errorMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881001 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal DetailedLocalOnly\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881002 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Webserver Error Pages - Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests must be selected\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver Error Pages Error Response Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'errorMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881002 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal CustomErrorPages\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'Custom'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","uuid":"67D2DE95-6BF8-1014-B241-DDE4996550FF","rule_id":"SV-218810r1022657","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Warning and error messages displayed to clients must be modified to minimize the identity of the IIS 10.0 web server, patches, loaded modules, and directory paths.","potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Error Pages\" icon.\n\nClick any error message, and then click \"Edit Feature Setting\" from the \"Actions\" Pane. This will apply to all error messages.\n\nSet Feature Setting to \"Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\" or \"Custom error pages\".","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nDouble-click the \"Error Pages\" icon.\nClick any error message, and then click \"Edit Feature Setting\" from the \"Actions\" Pane. This will apply to all error messages.\n\nIf the feature setting is not set to \"Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\", or \"Custom error pages\"  this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"Management\", double-click \"Management Service\".\n\nStop the Web Management Service under the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nConfigure only known, secure IP ranges as \"Allow\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" in \"Actions\" pane.\n\nRestart the Web Management Service under the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Note: This requirement applies to the Web Management Service. If the Web Management Service is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"Management\", double-click \"Management Service\".\n\nIf \"Enable remote connections\" is not selected, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf \"Enable remote connections\" is selected, review the entries under \"IP Address Restrictions\".\n\nVerify only known, secure IP ranges are configured as \"Allow\".\n\nIf \"IP Address Restrictions\" are not configured or IP ranges configured to \"Allow\" are not restrictive enough to prevent connections from nonsecure zones, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:4301"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218812r961278_rule","ccis":["CCI-002314"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Remote access to the web server is any access that communicates through an external, non-organization-controlled network. Remote access can be used to access hosted applications or to perform management functions.\n\nA web server can be accessed remotely and must be capable of restricting access from what the DoD defines as non-secure zones. Non-secure zones are defined as any IP, subnet, or region defined as a threat to the organization. The non-secure zones must be defined for public web servers logically located in a DMZ, as well as private web servers with perimeter protection devices. By restricting access from non-secure zones through internal web server access lists, the web server can stop or slow denial of service (DoS) attacks on the web server.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000315-WSR-000004","uuid":"67D2E5BB-6BF8-1014-B78E-CB7499827336","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must restrict inbound connections from non-secure zones.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218812r961278","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218812","title":"SRG-APP-000315-WSR-000004"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109263","V-100159"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000142","group_id_src":"V-218812","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218812"},{"rule_id":"SV-218813r961281","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must provide the capability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access to the hosted applications.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170","uuid":"67D2ED4D-6BF8-1014-A0AD-AD4E725CCCDD","discussion":"During an attack on the web server or any of the hosted applications, the system administrator may need to disconnect or disable access by users to stop the attack.\n\nThe web server must provide a capability to disconnect users to a hosted application without compromising other hosted applications unless deemed necessary to stop the attack. Methods to disconnect or disable connections are to stop the application service for a specified hosted application, stop the web server, or block all connections through web server access list.\n\nThe web server capabilities used to disconnect or disable users from connecting to hosted applications and the web server must be documented to make certain that, during an attack, the proper action is taken to conserve connectivity to any other hosted application if possible and to make certain log data is conserved for later forensic analysis.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218813, SV-218813r961281, SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170)\n","ccis":["CCI-002322"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:4501","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218813r961281_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator and Web Manager.\n\nAsk for documentation for the IIS 10.0 web server administration.\n\nVerify there are documented procedures for shutting down an IIS 10.0 website in the event of an attack. The procedure should, at a minimum, provide the following steps:\n\nDetermine the respective website for the application at risk of an attack.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\n\nSelect the respective website.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Website\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf necessary, stop all websites.\n\nIf necessary, stop the IIS 10.0 web server by selecting the web server in the IIS Manager.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Server\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf the web server is not capable or cannot be configured to disconnect or disable remote access to the hosted applications when necessary, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Prepare documented procedures for shutting down an IIS 10.0 website in the event of an attack.\n\nThe procedure should, at a minimum, provide the following steps:\n\nDetermine the respective website for the application at risk of an attack.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS Manager.\n\nSelect the respective website. \n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Website\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf necessary, stop all websites.\n\nIf necessary, stop the IIS 10.0 web server by selecting the web server in the IIS Manager.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Server\", click \"Stop\".","group_id":"V-218813","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218813","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000143","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218813","title":"SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109265","V-100161"],"comments":null,"mitigations":""},{"check_content":"Open Explorer and navigate to the inetpub directory.\n\nRight-click \"inetpub\" and select \"Properties\".\n\nClick the \"Security\" tab.\n\nVerify the permissions for the following users; if the permissions are less restrictive, this is a finding.\n\nSystem: Full control\nAdministrators: Full control\nTrustedInstaller: Full control\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group): Read and execute, This folder, subfolders and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group): Read and execute, This folder, subfolders and files\nUsers: Read and execute, list folder contents\nCREATOR OWNER: Full Control, Subfolders and files only","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open Explorer and navigate to the inetpub directory.\n\nRight-click \"inetpub\" and select \"Properties\".\n\nClick the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSet the following permissions: \nSystem: Full control\nAdministrators: Full control\nTrustedInstaller: Full control\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group): Read and execute, This folder, subfolders and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group): Read and execute, This folder, subfolders and files\nUsers: Read and execute, list folder contents\nCREATOR OWNER: Full Control, Subfolders and files only","uuid":"67D2F42E-6BF8-1014-976D-81CCBF61B7D4","group_title":"SRG-APP-000340-WSR-000029","rule_id":"SV-218814r1067589","rule_title":"IIS 10.0 web server system files must conform to minimum file permission requirements.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218814","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218814r1067589_rule","discussion":"This check verifies the key web server system configuration files are owned by the SA or the web administrator controlled account. These same files that control the configuration of the web server, and thus its behavior, must also be accessible by the account running the web service. If these files are altered by a malicious user, the web server would no longer be under the control of its managers and owners; properties in the web server configuration could be altered to compromise the entire server platform.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The inetpub directory must conform to minimum file permission requirements.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881401 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The inetpub directory must conform to minimum file permission requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881401 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command on inetpub directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      : for command, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     command must be equal to 'icacls C:\\inetpub'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881401 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Permissions must equal expected output\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls C:\\inetpub'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\inetpub NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Administrators:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Users:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           CREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000144","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109267","V-100163"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000340-WSR-000029","id":"V-218814"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218814","group_id":"V-218814","severity":"medium"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-218815r961392_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218815"},"ccis":["CCI-001849"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The IIS 10.0 web server must use a logging mechanism that is configured to allocate log record storage capacity large enough to accommodate the logging requirements of the IIS 10.0 web server.e)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881501 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The IIS 10.0 web server must use a logging mechanism that is configured to allocate log record storage capacity large enough to accommodate the logging requirements of the IIS 10.0 web server.e\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881501 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver default logfile rollover setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.logFile.period'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881501 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : remove MIME types for OS shell program extensions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must not be equal to 'MaxSize'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.logFile.period'\n                        : result equals 'Daily'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"To ensure the logging mechanism used by the web server has sufficient storage capacity in which to write the logs, the logging mechanism must be able to allocate log record storage capacity.\n\nThe task of allocating log record storage capacity is usually performed during initial installation of the logging mechanism. The system administrator will usually coordinate the allocation of physical drive space with the web server administrator along with the physical location of the partition and disk. Refer to NIST SP 800-92 for specific requirements on log rotation and storage dependent on the impact of the web server.","uuid":"67D2FB3A-6BF8-1014-8540-DE4E5BF46FF1","group_title":"SRG-APP-000357-WSR-000150","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must use a logging mechanism configured to allocate log record storage capacity large enough to accommodate the logging requirements of the IIS 10.0 web server.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218815r961392","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"IIS\" double-click on the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nIf necessary, in the \"Logging\" configuration box, re-designate a log path to a location able to house the logs.\n\nUnder \"Log File Rollover\", de-select the \"Do not create new log files\" setting.\n\nConfigure a schedule to rollover log files on a regular basis.","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"IIS\" double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nIn the \"Logging\" configuration box, determine the \"Directory:\" to which the \"W3C\" logging is being written.\n\nConfirm with the System Administrator that the designated log path is of sufficient size to maintain the logging.\n\nUnder \"Log File Rollover\", verify \"Do not create new log files\" is not selected.\n\nVerify a schedule is configured to rollover log files on a regular basis.\n\nConsult with the System Administrator to determine if there is a documented process for moving the log files off of the IIS 10.0 web server to another logging device.\n\nIf the designated logging path device is not of sufficient space to maintain all log files, and there is not a schedule to rollover files on a regular basis, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218815","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218815","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109269","V-100165"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000357-WSR-000150","id":"V-218815"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000145","weight":"10.0"},{"rule_id":"SV-218816r1067591","rule_title":"Access to web administration tools must be restricted to the web manager and the web managers designees.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D3025D-6BF8-1014-8C41-A37F87925931","group_title":"SRG-APP-000380-WSR-000072","discussion":"A web server can be modified through parameter modification, patch installation, upgrades to the web server or modules, and security parameter changes. With each of these changes, there is the potential for an adverse effect such as a DoS, web server instability, or hosted application instability.\n\nTo limit changes to the web server and limit exposure to any adverse effects from the changes, files such as the web server application files, libraries, and configuration files must have permissions and ownership set properly to only allow privileged users access.\n\nThe key web service administrative and configuration tools must only be accessible by the web server staff. All users granted this authority will be documented and approved by the ISSO. Access to the IIS Manager will be limited to authorized users and administrators.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000380-WSR-000072, SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000147, SRG-APP-000033-WSR-000169","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218816, SV-218816r1067591, SRG-APP-000380-WSR-000072)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213","CCI-001813","CCI-002385"],"rule_id_src":"SV-218816r1067591_rule","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:5101"},"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Right-click \"InetMgr.exe\", then click \"Properties\" from the \"Context\" menu.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nReview the groups and user names.\n\nThe following accounts may have Full control privileges:\n\nTrustedInstaller\nWeb Managers\nWeb Manager designees\nCREATOR OWNER\n\nThe following accounts may have read and execute, or read permissions:\n\nNon Web Manager Administrators\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group)\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES (built-in security group)\nSYSTEM\nUsers\n\nSpecific users may be granted read and execute and read permissions.\n\nCompare the local documentation authorizing specific users, against the users observed when reviewing the groups and users.\n\nIf any other access is observed, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Restrict access to the web administration tool to only the web manager and the web managerâs designees.","group_id":"V-218816","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218816","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000147","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109271","V-100167"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218816","title":"SRG-APP-000380-WSR-000072"},"mitigations":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove all unapproved programs and roles from the production web server.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Review programs installed on the OS.\n\nOpen Control Panel.\n\nOpen Programs and Features.\n\nThe following programs may be installed without any additional documentation:\n\nAdministration Pack for IIS\nIIS Search Engine Optimization Toolkit\nMicrosoft .NET Framework version 3.5 SP1 or greater\nMicrosoft Web Platform Installer version 3.x or greater\nVirtual Machine Additions\n\nReview the installed programs, if any programs are installed other than those listed above, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If additional software is needed and has supporting documentation signed by the ISSO, this is not a finding.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218817, SV-218817r961470, SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Web servers provide numerous processes, features, and functionalities that utilize TCP/IP ports. Some of these processes may be deemed unnecessary or too unsecure to run on a production system.\n\nThe web server must provide the capability to disable or deactivate network-related services deemed non-essential to the server mission, are too unsecure, or are prohibited by the PPSM CAL and vulnerability assessments.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:5301"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218817r961470_rule","ccis":["CCI-001762"],"rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must not be running on a system providing any other role.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218817r961470","uuid":"67D30939-6BF8-1014-B1BF-89E3F9CDF9D4","group_title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109273","V-100169"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218817","title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175"},"rule_version":"IIST-SV-000148","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218817","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218817","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3"},{"mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109275","V-100171"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218818","title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000149","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218818","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218818","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Click âStartâ, click âAdministrative Toolsâ, and then click âServer Managerâ.\n\nExpand the roles node, right-click âPrint Servicesâ, and then select âRemove Roles Servicesâ.\n\nIf the Internet Printing option is checked, clear the check box, click âNextâ, and then click âRemoveâ to complete the wizard.","check_content":"If the Print Services role and the Internet Printing role are not installed, this check is Not Applicable.\n\nNavigate to the following directory:\n\n%windir%\\web\\printers\n\nIf this folder exists, this is a finding.\n\nDetermine whether Internet Printing is enabled:\n\nClick âStartâ, click âAdministrative Toolsâ, and then click âServer Managerâ.\n\nExpand the roles node, right-click âPrint Servicesâ, and then select âRemove Roles Servicesâ.\n\nIf the Internet Printing option is enabled, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-218818r961470_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218818"},"ccis":["CCI-001762"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The use of IPP on an IIS web server allows client access to shared printers. This privileged access could allow remote code execution by increasing the web servers attack surface. Additionally, since IPP does not support SSL, it is considered a risk and will not be deployed.","uuid":"67D31574-6BF8-1014-8DF2-BB2D7614B34E","group_title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The Internet Printing Protocol (IPP) must be disabled on the IIS 10.0 web server.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218818r961470"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000148","id":"V-218819"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109277","V-100173"],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000151","reference_identifier":"4052","group_id":"V-218819","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218819","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server registry.\n\nVerify the following keys are present and configured. The required setting depends upon the requirements of the application. These settings must be explicitly configured to show a conscientious tuning has been made.\n\nNavigate to HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\\n\nConfigure the following registry keys to levels to accommodate the hosted applications.\n\nCreate REG_DWORD \"URIEnableCache\"\nCreate REG_DWORD \"UriMaxUriBytes\"\nCreate REG_DWORD \"UriScavengerPeriod\"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the IIS 10.0 web server is not hosting any applications, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is hosting applications, consult with the system administrator to determine risk analysis performed when the application was written and deployed to the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nObtain documentation on the configuration.\nVerify, at a minimum, the following tuning settings in the registry.\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server registry.\nVerify the following keys are present and configured. The required setting depends upon the requirements of the application. \nRecommended settings are not provided as these settings must be explicitly configured to show a conscientious tuning has been made.\nNavigate to HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\\nREG_DWORD \"URIEnableCache\"\nREG_DWORD \"UriMaxUriBytes\"\nREG_DWORD \"UriScavengerPeriod\"\n\nIf explicit settings are not configured for \"URIEnableCache\", \"UriMaxUriBytes\" and \"UriScavengerPeriod\", this is a finding.","discussion":"A Denial of Service (DoS) can occur when the web server is overwhelmed and can no longer respond to additional requests. A web server not properly tuned may become overwhelmed and cause a DoS condition even with expected traffic from users. To avoid a DoS, the web server must be tuned to handle the expected traffic for the hosted applications.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false ((1 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: URIEnableCache)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\URIEnableCache'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((2 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriMaxUriBytes)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\UriMaxUriBytes'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((3 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriScavengerPeriod)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\UriScavengerPeriod'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881901 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (1 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: URIEnableCache\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881901 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (1 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: URIEnableCache\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'URIEnableCache'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\URIEnableCache'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881902 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (2 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriMaxUriBytes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881902 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (2 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriMaxUriBytes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'UriMaxUriBytes'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\UriMaxUriBytes'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21881903 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (3 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriScavengerPeriod\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21881903 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (3 of 3) The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application. Regkey: UriScavengerPeriod\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'UriScavengerPeriod'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21881901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\UriScavengerPeriod'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","ccis":["CCI-002385"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218819"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218819r1022659_rule","rule_id":"SV-218819r1022659","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the hosted application.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000148","uuid":"67D31DE4-6BF8-1014-9EC4-FC16BFFCB493"},{"stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218820","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218820","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000152","id":"V-218820"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109279","V-100175"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000152","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218820"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218820r961632_rule","discussion":"The HTTP protocol is a stateless protocol. To maintain a session, a session identifier is used. The session identifier is a piece of data used to identify a session and a user. If the session identifier is compromised by an attacker, the session can be hijacked. By encrypting the session identifier, the identifier becomes more difficult for an attacker to hijack, decrypt, and use before the session has expired.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The IIS 10.0 web server must have keepSessionIdSecure set to True)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882001 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The IIS 10.0 web server must have keepSessionIdSecure set to True\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver KeepSessionIDSecure Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/asp'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882001 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/asp'\n                        : parameter equals 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000152","uuid":"67D324F5-6BF8-1014-99BB-84906B3C98F0","rule_id":"SV-218820r961632","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"IIS 10.0 web server session IDs must be sent to the client using TLS.","potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.webServer/asp\".\n\nExpand the \"session\" section.\n\nSelect \"True\" for the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" setting.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nUnder the \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.webServer/asp\".\n\nExpand the \"session\" section.\n\nVerify the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" is set to \"True\".\n\nIf the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" is not set to \"True\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-109281","V-100177"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000156","id":"V-218821"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000153","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","group_id":"V-218821","severity":"high","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218821","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server.\n\nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server \n\nCreate a REG_DWORD named \"DisabledByDefault\" with a value of \"0\".\nCreate a REG_DWORD named \"Enabled\" with a  value of \"1\".\n\nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\n\nFor each protocol:\nCreate a REG_DWORD named \"DisabledByDefault\" with a value of \"1\".\nCreate a REG_DWORD named \"Enabled\" with a  value of \"0\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server.\n\nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server\n\nVerify a REG_DWORD value of \"0\" for \"DisabledByDefault\".\nVerify a REG_DWORD value of \"1\" for \"Enabled\".\n\nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\n\nVerify a REG_DWORD value of \"1\" for \"DisabledByDefault\".\nVerify a REG_DWORD value of \"0\" for \"Enabled\".\n\nIf any of the respective registry paths do not exist or are configured with the wrong value, this is a finding.\n\nSSL 3.0 is disabled by default in newer Operating Systems. If SSL 3.0 has a registry DWORD enabled with a value of 1, this is a finding. If this key is not present, this is not a finding.","discussion":"TLS encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2-approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.\n\nNIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.2 DisabledByDefault set to 0) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for DisabledByDefault.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.2 Enabled set to 1) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 1 for Enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.1 Disabled) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for Enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.1 DisabledByDefault) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 1 for DisabledByDefault.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.0 Disabled) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for Enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((TLS 1.0 DisabledByDefault) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 1 for DisabledByDefault.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((SSL 3.0 Disabled) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for Enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false ((SSL 3.0 DisabledByDefault) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 1 for DisabledByDefault.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882101 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (TLS 1.2 DisabledByDefault set to 0) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for DisabledByDefault.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match th