               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882105 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (TLS 1.0 DisabledByDefault)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisabledByDefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882102 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To One\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882108 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (SSL 3.0 Disabled) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 0 for Enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882108 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (SSL 3.0 Disabled)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882101 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To Zero\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882109 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : (SSL 3.0 DisabledByDefault) Access the IIS 10.0 Web Server. HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server. Verify a REG_DWORD value of 1 for DisabledByDefault.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882109 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : (SSL 3.0 DisabledByDefault)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisabledByDefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882102 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To One\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218821"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218821r1067596_rule","rule_id":"SV-218821r1067596","rule_title":"An IIS 10.0 web server must maintain the confidentiality of controlled information during transmission through the use of an approved Transport Layer Security (TLS) version.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D32C3F-6BF8-1014-8780-B943F90BE30F","group_title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000156"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Review the web server documentation and deployed configuration to determine which version of TLS is being used.\n\nIf the TLS version is not TLS 1.2 or higher, according to NIST SP 800-52, or if non-FIPS-approved algorithms are enabled, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Configure the web server to use an approved TLS version according to NIST SP 800-52 and to disable all non-approved versions.","documentable":"false","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must maintain the confidentiality of controlled information during transmission through the use of an approved Transport Layer Security (TLS) version.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218822r961632","group_title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000156","uuid":"67D33373-6BF8-1014-AD65-F0DA321D54C2","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218822, SV-218822r961632, SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000156)\n","discussion":"TLS is a required transmission protocol for a web server hosting controlled information. The use of TLS provides confidentiality of data in transit between the web server and client. FIPS 140-2-approved TLS versions must be enabled and non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.\n\nNIST SP 800-52 defines the approved TLS versions for government applications.","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218822r961632_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:6301","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-002418"],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000154","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000156","id":"V-218822"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109283","V-100179"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218822","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218822","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218823","title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109285","V-100181"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000156","reference_identifier":"4052","group_id":"V-218823","severity":"high","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218823","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nAccess the \"Apps\" menu. Under Administrative Tools, select Computer Management.\n\nIn left pane, expand \"Local Users and Groups\" and click on \"Users\".\n\nChange passwords for any local accounts present that are used by IIS 10.0, then verify with System Administrator default passwords have been changed.\n\nDevelop an internal process for changing passwords on a regular basis.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Access the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nAccess the \"Apps\" menu. Under \"Administrative Tools\", select \"Computer Management\".\n\nIn left pane, expand \"Local Users and Groups\" and click \"Users\".\n\nReview the local users listed in the middle pane. \n\nIf any local accounts are present and used by IIS 10.0, verify with System Administrator that default passwords have been changed.\n\nIf passwords have not been changed from the default, this is a finding.","discussion":"During installation of the web server software, accounts are created for the web server to operate properly. The accounts installed can have either no password installed or a default password, which will be known and documented by the vendor and the user community.\n\nThe first things an attacker will try when presented with a logon screen are the default user identifiers with default passwords. Installed applications may also install accounts with no password, making the logon even easier. Once the web server is installed, the passwords for any created accounts should be changed and documented. The new passwords must meet the requirements for all passwords, i.e., upper/lower characters, numbers, special characters, time until change, reuse policy, etc.\n\nService accounts or system accounts that have no logon capability do not need to have passwords set or changed.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-218823, SV-218823r961863, SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079)\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:6501"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218823r961863_rule","rule_id":"SV-218823r961863","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"All accounts installed with the IIS 10.0 web server software and tools must have passwords assigned and default passwords changed.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079","uuid":"67D33ABF-6BF8-1014-8C87-9BEC3AF95993"},{"reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000158","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218824"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109287","V-100183"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218824","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218824","check_content":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"ISAPI and CGI restrictions\" icon.\n\nClick âEdit Feature Settings\".\n\nVerify the \"Allow unspecified CGI modules\" and the \"Allow unspecified ISAPI modules\" check boxes are NOT checked.\n\nIf either or both of the \"Allow unspecified CGI modules\" and the \"Allow unspecified ISAPI modules\" check boxes are checked, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \"ISAPI and CGI restrictions\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\".\n\nRemove the check from the \"Allow unspecified CGI modules\" and the \"Allow unspecified ISAPI modules\" check boxes.\n\nClick \"OK\".","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","uuid":"67D341AE-6BF8-1014-A15E-EE38DF77551A","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Unspecified file extensions on a production IIS 10.0 web server must be removed.","rule_id":"SV-218824r961863","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218824"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218824r961863_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (1 of 2))\nTest                    :   true (Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (2 of 2))\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882401 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (1 of 2)\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882401 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (1 of 2)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/security/isapiCgiRestriction'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'notListedIsapisAllowed'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882401 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/security/isapiCgiRestriction'\n                        : parameter equals 'notListedIsapisAllowed'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882402 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (2 of 2)\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882402 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Unspecified file extensions must not be allowed to execute on the production web server. (2 of 2)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/security/isapiCgiRestriction'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'notListedCgisAllowed'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882401 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/security/isapiCgiRestriction'\n                        : parameter equals 'notListedCgisAllowed'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","discussion":"By allowing unspecified file extensions to execute, the web servers attack surface is significantly increased. This increased risk can be reduced by only allowing specific ISAPI extensions or CGI extensions to run on the web server."},{"reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000159","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218825","title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109289","V-100185"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218825","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218825","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the Server is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server is hosting Exchange, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server is public facing, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the website is behind a load balancer or proxy server, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nDouble-click the \".NET Authorization Rules\" icon.\nEnsure \"All Users\" is set to \"Allow\", and \"Anonymous Users\" is set to \"Deny\", otherwise this is a finding.\nIf any other rules are present, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nDouble-click the \".NET Authorization Rules\" icon.\n\nAlter the list as necessary to ensure \"All Users\" is set to \"Allow\" and \"Anonymous Users\" is set to \"Deny\".\n\nRemove any other line items.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","uuid":"67D3552E-6BF8-1014-9E15-A0E1002756B9","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must have a global authorization rule configured to restrict access.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218825r1067593","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218825","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-218825r1067593_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Authorization rules can be configured at the server, website, folder (including Virtual Directories), or file level. It is recommended that URL Authorization be configured to only grant access to the necessary security principals. Configuring a global Authorization rule that restricts access ensures inheritance of the settings down through the hierarchy of web directories. This will ensure access to current and future content is only granted to the appropriate principals, mitigating risk of unauthorized access. "},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218826","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218826","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000200","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109291","V-100187"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000001-WSR-000001","id":"V-218826"},"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 websites MaxConnections setting must be configured to limit the number of allowed simultaneous session requests.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218826r960735","uuid":"67D3664E-6BF8-1014-8069-ECFC8BB4FE7A","group_title":"SRG-APP-000001-WSR-000001","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Access the IIS 10.0 IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 server. Select 'Configuration Editor' under the 'Management' section. From the 'Section:' drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate 'system.applicationHost/sites'. Expand 'siteDefaults'. Expand 'limits'. Review the results and verify the value is greater than zero for the 'maxconnections' parameter. If the maxconnections parameter is set to zero, this is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882601 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Access the IIS 10.0 IIS Manager. Click the IIS 10.0 server. Select 'Configuration Editor' under the 'Management' section. From the 'Section:' drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate 'system.applicationHost/sites'. Expand 'siteDefaults'. Expand 'limits'. Review the results and verify the value is greater than zero for the 'maxconnections' parameter. If the maxconnections parameter is set to zero, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882601 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver default maxconnections setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.limits.maxConnections'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882601 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must not equal zero\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must not be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.limits.maxConnections'\n                        : result equals '4294967295'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Resource exhaustion can occur when an unlimited number of concurrent requests are allowed on a website, facilitating a Denial of Service (DoS) attack. Mitigating this kind of attack will include limiting the number of concurrent HTTP/HTTPS requests per IP address and may include, where feasible, limiting parameter values associated with keepalive (i.e., a parameter used to limit the amount of time a connection may be inactive).","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218826"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218826r960735_rule","ccis":["CCI-000054"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Access the IIS 10.0 IIS Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 server.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.applicationHost/sites\".\n\nExpand \"siteDefaults\".\nExpand \"limits\".\n\nReview the results and verify the value is greater than zero for the \"maxconnections\" parameter.\n\nIf the maxconnections parameter is set to zero, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the IIS 10.0 IIS Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 server.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.applicationHost/sites\".\n\nExpand \"siteDefaults\".\nExpand \"limits\".\n\nSet the \"maxconnections\" parameter to a value greater than zero."},{"severity":"low","group_id":"V-218827","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218827","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109293","V-100189"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218827"},"rule_version":"IIST-SV-000205","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.enabled, verify that value equals true.)\nResult Analysis         :        Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.enabled = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \nTest                    :   false (Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains, verify that value is set to True.)\nResult Analysis         :        Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \nTest                    :   false (Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.max-age, verify that value is set to 1.)\nResult Analysis         :        Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.max-age = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps, verify that value is set to True. )\nResult Analysis         :        Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882701 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.enabled, verify that value equals true.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882701 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver keepSessionIdSecure setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.hsts.enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882701 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.hsts.enabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nResult Analysis         : Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.enabled = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882702 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains, verify that value is set to True.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882702 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver keepSessionIdSecure setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882701 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nResult Analysis         : Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.includeSubDomains = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882703 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.max-age, verify that value is set to 1.\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882703 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver keepSessionIdSecure setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.hsts.max-age'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882703 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must greater than zero\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.hsts.max-age'\n                        : result equals '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.max-age = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:21882704 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check that system.applicationHost/sites:siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps, verify that value is set to True. \nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:21882704 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Webserver keepSessionIdSecure setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Webserver'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.applicationHost/sites'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:21882701 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Webserver'\n                        : section equals 'system.applicationHost/sites'\n                        : parameter equals 'siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nResult Analysis         : Webserver//system.applicationHost/sites/siteDefaults.hsts.redirectHttpToHttps = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) ensures browsers always connect to a website over TLS. HSTS exists to remove the need for redirection configurations. HSTS relies on the browser, web server, and a public \"Allowlist\". If the browser does not support HSTS, it will be ignored.","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:218827"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218827r1192779_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 web server must enable HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS).","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218827r1192779","uuid":"67D37040-6BF8-1014-B171-B131FC935770","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Using the Configuration Editor in the IIS Manager or Powershell:\nEnable HSTS.\nSet includeSubDomains to True.\nSet max-age to a value greater than 0.\nSet redirectHttpToHttps to True.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server is providing OCSP or CRL, and not otherwise hosting any content, this is not applicable.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 Web Server.\nOpen IIS Manager.\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\nOpen on Configuration Editor under Management.\nFor the Section, navigate to system.applicationHost/sites.\nExpand siteDefaults and HSTS.\nIf enabled is not set to True, this is a finding.\nIf includeSubDomains is not set to True, this is a finding.\nIf max-age is not set to a value greater than 0, this is a finding.\nIf redirectHttpToHttps is not True, this is a finding.\n\nIf the website is behind a load balancer or proxy server, and HSTS enablement is handled there, this is not applicable.\n\nIf the version of Windows Server does not natively support HSTS, this is not a finding."},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-228572","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-228572","reference_identifier":"4052","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000160","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["V-102895","SV-111857"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-228572","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075"},"classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"67D3791D-6BF8-1014-B201-FC74EF5AC07F","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"An IIS Server configured to be a SMTP relay must require authentication.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-228572r960963","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-228572r960963_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.0.server:questionnaire:7501"},"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-228572, SV-228572r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Anonymous SMTP relays are strictly prohibited. An anonymous SMTP relay can be a vector for many types of malicious activity not limited to server exploitation for the sending of SPAM mail, access to emails, phishing, DoS attacks, etc. Enabling TLS, authentication, and strictly assigning IP addresses that can communicate with the relay greatly reduce the risk of the implementation.","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator about the role of the IIS 10.0 web server.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 web server is running SMTP relay services, have the SA provide supporting documentation on how the server is hardened. A DoD-issued certificate, and specific allowed IP address should be configured.\n\nIf the IIS web server is not running SMTP relay services, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the IIS web server running SMTP relay services without TLS enabled, this is a finding.\n\nIf the IIS web server running SMTP relay services is not configured to only allow a specific IP address, from the same network as the relay, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the relay server with a specific allowed IP address, from the same network as the relay, and implement TLS.","documentable":"false"},{"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:241789"},"rule_id_src":"SV-241789r1022662_rule","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"HTTP Response Headers contain information that could enable an attacker to gain access to an information system. Failure to prevent the sending of certain HTTP Response Header information to remote requesters exposes internal configuration information to potential attackers.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","uuid":"67D3819B-6BF8-1014-A24C-DAC36EF43854","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"ASP.NET version must be removed from the HTTP Response Header information.","rule_id":"SV-241789r1022662","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nUnder the \"Connections\" pane on the left side of the management console, select the IIS 10.0 web server.\nClick the HTTP Response Headers button.\nClick to select the âX-Powered-Byâ HTTP Header.\nClick âRemoveâ in the Actions Panel.\nNote: This can be performed multiple ways, this is an example.","documentable":"false","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nUnder the \"Connections\" pane on the left side of the management console, select the IIS 10.0 web server.\nClick the HTTP Response Headers button.\nClick to select the âX-Powered-Byâ HTTP Header.\nIf âX-Powered-Byâ has not been removed, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-241789","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","responsibility":"","severity":"low","group_id":"V-241789","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","id":"V-241789"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-54431","V-41854"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4052","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000215"},{"group_id":"V-268325","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-268325","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"IIST-SV-000220","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4052","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109223","V-100119"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000015","id":"V-268325"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-268325r1025163","rule_title":"The Request Smuggling filter must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"67D38A1C-6BF8-1014-B4A4-8723A0092CA4","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000015","discussion":"Security scans show Request Smuggling vulnerability on IIS server.\n\nThe vulnerability allows a remote attacker to perform HTTP request smuggling attack.\n\nThe vulnerability exists due to the way that HTTP proxies (front-end) and web servers (back-end) that do not strictly adhere to RFC standards handle sequences of HTTP requests received from multiple sources. A remote attacker can send a specially crafted request to a targeted IIS Server, perform HTTP request smuggling attack and modify responses or retrieve information from another user's HTTP session.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:55\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters key (REG_DWORD): DisableRequestSmuggling = 1)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\DisableRequestSmuggling'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:tst:26832501 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters key (REG_DWORD): DisableRequestSmuggling = 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:obj:26832501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\DisableRequestSmuggling\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableRequestSmuggling'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:ste:26832501 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To One\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\DisableRequestSmuggling'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.0.server:def:268325","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Server_V3R6_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-268325r1025163_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open Registry Editor.\nNavigate to \"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\"\nVerify \"DisableRequestSmugglingâ is set to \"1\".\n\nIf REG_DWORD DisableRequestSmuggling is not set to 1, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Navigate to \"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\".\nCreate REG_DWORD \"DisableRequestSmugglingâ and set it to \"1\".\n\nNote: This can be performed multiple ways; this is an example."}],"stig_name":"Microsoft IIS 10.0 Server Security Technical Implementation Guide","classification":"UNCLASSIFIED","version":"3","reference_identifier":"4052","uuid":"67CFE620-6BF8-1014-B537-E86039D2C5A3","release_info":"Release: 7 Benchmark Date: 01 Apr 2026"}],"title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T13:07:35","cklb_version":"1.0"}